From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: phy: add MT6873 UFS PHY fallback

The MT6873 UFS M-PHY has the same register window as the MT8183 binding.
Vendor LK performs the device-specific efuse and TX calibration before
handoff, while the vendor 4.14 kernel M-PHY init hook is a no-op.  Use an
MT6873-specific compatible with an MT8183 fallback for the initial mainline
power/clock probe.

This does not establish that the MT8183 PHY power sequence covers every
MT6873 calibration or power-state transition.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,ufs-phy.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,ufs-phy.yaml
index 3e62b5d..70c289f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,ufs-phy.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/mediatek,ufs-phy.yaml
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ properties:
     oneOf:
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - mediatek,mt6873-ufsphy
               - mediatek,mt8195-ufsphy
           - const: mediatek,mt8183-ufsphy
       - const: mediatek,mt8183-ufsphy
-- 
